<http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/bdefa7d0-308a-426a-9b12-d60cd2d3c05b-01/NonDisclosureAgreementTerm$_ContractNotice1_ProcurementProjectLot1_TenderingTerms1>
  a epo:NonDisclosureAgreementTerm;
  epo:isNonDisclosureAgreementRequired true;
  dct:description """TenneT is a leading cross-border Transmission
                    System Operator (TSO) responsible for the secure and reliable transmission of
                    electricity across large parts of the Netherlands and Germany. TenneT plays a
                    critical role in enabling the energy transition in Northwest Europe through
                    large-scale grid development, digitalisation, security-by-design, and lifecycle
                    resilience. As part of this strategic roadmap, TenneT relies on a broad and
                    continuously evolving software ecosystem with solutions sourced from numerous
                    vendors and licensing constructs.

                    This consultation does not constitute a call for competition, request for
                    quotation, pre-qualification activity, or any part of the actual procurement
                    procedure. No legal, financial, or commercial rights may be derived from this
                    document or participation herein. Participation is voluntary.

                    Furthermore, in accordance with the EU Procurement Directives and the Dutch
                    Aanbestedingswet 2012, this market consultation is conducted to ensure early,
                    transparent and non-discriminatory interaction with the market. All engagement
                    activities will strictly avoid providing any party with a competitive advantage
                    in the subsequent tender procedure.
                    This consultation also serves as an early engagement mechanism to ensure that
                    TenneT’s future tendering approach aligns with current market capabilities and
                    anticipated developments in the European landscape.

                    The market consultation will take place digitally via the Mercell platform."""@en,
    "This is requirement for the EU tender."@nl .

